  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The Back Door – pass from behind the goal and a shot at full speed",
  "description": "Half court, one goal with a goalkeeper. Three lines: A with the balls by the left boards near the centre line, B in the left corner and C by the right boards near the centre line. A carries the ball a few metres and passes on the move to B. B takes the ball behind the goal and passes it out on the other side to C, who arrives at full speed and shoots from a bit further out. After the pass A carries on in front of goal and goes for the rebound.\n\nRotation: A to the B line, B to the C line and C to the A line. Switch sides after a few minutes.\n\nVariant: after the pass B steps in and defends against A in front of goal. C can then choose between a shot and a pass in to A. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "C: start in time to reach the shooting spot at the same moment as the pass."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Shoot at full speed – don't stop to shoot."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "B: look up behind the goal and put the pass in front of C."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "A: get to where the rebound will land, stick on the floor."
    }
  ],
